---
description: Wobbrik branch, commit, local review and local CI delivery rules
alwaysApply: true
---

- Follow AGENTS.md section “Branch, commit və lokal CI” for every change.
- Use a focused feat/, fix/, chore/ or docs/ branch and meaningful commits.
- Review the final diff locally and record findings in docs/reviews/.
- Run ./scripts/local-ci.sh only on main after merging the reviewed branch. Never run CI on feature/fix/docs/chore branches.
- Do not add GitHub CI. Never treat skipped or failed checks as passing.
- Merge after successful local review, preserving branch history; then run CI on main. Fix failures on a separate branch, review and merge it, then rerun CI on main. Failed main CI means delivery is incomplete.
- Backend changes need their own branch, review and required backend checks.
